# Virtual pads, foreign devices and the uaccess tag (06-input.md section 3, rules 1 and 3; RUY-446,
# RUY-1063). 70-ruya-input.rules leaves ruya-inputd's virtual pads (marked, phys ruya-input/pad<n>)
# and every foreign device untagged, but systemd's 70-uaccess.rules sorts after it and tags every
# joystick. That made logind give the seat's user, ruya-shell, an ACL entry on the node. This file
# sorts after 70-uaccess.rules and before 73-seat-late.rules (which applies the ACL), so the tag is
# gone when logind looks. A foreign device also loses power-switch (70-power-switch.rules tags every
# key device): logind must not take a power key from a device a profile made. ruya-inputd's other
# devices (the navigation keyboard) and hardware are not matched: they keep uaccess.
SUBSYSTEM!="input", GOTO="ruya_input_pad_end"
KERNEL!="event*", GOTO="ruya_input_pad_end"
ENV{RUYA_INPUT_ORIGIN}=="foreign", TAG-="uaccess", TAG-="power-switch", OWNER="ruya-input", MODE="0600", GOTO="ruya_input_pad_end"
ENV{RUYA_INPUT_ORIGIN}=="own", ATTRS{phys}=="ruya-input/pad*", TAG-="uaccess", OWNER="ruya-input", MODE="0600"
LABEL="ruya_input_pad_end"
